# Python
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.venv/
.venv312/
.ipynb_checkpoints/

# RULE FOR THIS FILE: ignore DATA, never CODE.
# Source lives in src/ and is always tracked. Where an ignore rule covers a
# directory that could ever hold a .py, the rule is written as `dir/*` with an
# explicit `!dir/*.py` so git can still descend and see the source. A bare
# `dir/` stops git descending at all, which would swallow code silently.

# Pipeline inputs/outputs -- regenerate with preprocessing.py
dataset/raw/
dataset/processed/*
models/
catboost_info/

# EXCEPTION: the train/val/test split. These three files are 4 KB total and
# are the ONE clinical artefact the MRI stream cannot do without -- m2_index.py
# reads them to assign each scan a split, and both streams must use the same
# assignment or fusion leaks across splits. Everything else in dataset/processed/
# is rebuildable from dataset/raw/, but dataset/raw/ is 752 MB of ADNI tables
# that a machine set up only for the MRI work will not have. Tracking them makes
# the repo clonable onto an MRI-only machine.
!dataset/processed/train_rids.csv
!dataset/processed/val_rids.csv
!dataset/processed/test_rids.csv

# Preprocessed MRI volumes: ~1.8 GB now, ~4.6 GB at the full cohort, and
# DUA-restricted subject data. Written as `*` rather than `mri_prep/` so that
# any helper script dropped in here stays visible to git.
dataset/mri_prep/*
!dataset/mri_prep/*.py

# MRI download area.
# Deny by default: this directory fills with ~27 GB of zips and, after
# unpacking, one NIfTI per subject in dataset/mri_raw/<PTID>/. Only the
# small provenance artefacts below are worth tracking, so new files are
# ignored unless explicitly allowed.
dataset/mri_raw/*
!dataset/mri_raw/*.py
!dataset/mri_raw/selected_scans.csv
!dataset/mri_raw/selected_image_ids.txt
!dataset/mri_raw/ida_search_results_baselineT1.csv

# NEVER commit: _zips/zip_urls.txt holds pre-authenticated IDA download
# URLs. Those UUID links grant the collection to anyone who has them,
# with no login. Covered by the deny-by-default rule above; named here so
# it does not get whitelisted back in by accident.
dataset/mri_raw/_zips/

# Outbound data bundles (multi-GB, ADNI DUA-restricted - never commit)
dataset/*.tar
dataset/*.tar.*
